"_doc": [
  "The IMR instance's fish layer (tools/instance.json layer.fish; design note docs/reviews/2026-11-14-sheet-overlay-design.md v2, step 5): what IMR decides about its fish content, laid on tools/fish_source.json (the sources' part) by tools/build_fish.py through tools/instance.py fish_source. Edit this file, then re-run the build: python3 tools/build_fish.py --regroup (offline) is enough for slides, cues, look, phase, the IMR tag, an entry's IMR name and family, a species' common name and section, start and the look groups; a circle, or a species' pdf or cs (the IMR list), needs the full build. The content editor's edits are not here: curation.json content, laid over at load (rule A1). Layout: tools/instance.py layer_dumps (one node per line).",
  "start: the starter core, the circle-1 entries a new player meets first, before any other opens (model.js openPick, a record's first). Pierre's fish-ID design (2026-11-04): four easy, readable families first, Butterflyfishes, Angelfishes, Damselfishes & Anemonefishes, Surgeonfishes & Tangs.",
  "look: look-alike groups of the book's families declared beyond the IMR course, each {src, key (the key whose family labels the ids name: applied only while it is in force), groups [[family ids]], note {\"a|b\": words}}: every pair of a group is a look-alike both ways, its source in the families' lsrc (tools/build_fish.py add_families). Pierre, 2026-11-06, from experience; they seed the traps and the confusion groups until pooled fish answers exist.",
  "nodes: {teaching node or sub-entry id (tools/fish_source.json teach, sub): its fields}. A node or sub-entry the source does not hold stops the build.",
  "  circle (teaching nodes only; a species takes its node's circle, Q214): 1 IMR core, 2 seen sometimes on SVS video, 3 opt-in beyond IMR; absent: 1.",
  "  src (teaching nodes only): \"imr\", the IMR tag of the entries of the IMR fish presentation (fish.json families imr, the entry's name as IMR writes it); the other sources (pdf, diver, wink) stay in tools/fish_source.json.",
  "  sign (teaching nodes only): false when the entry is taught but not on the presentation's dive-sign list.",
  "  name, fam (only on an entry this file tags imr, and name on its sub-entries): the entry's name as IMR writes it and the family as IMR spells it (fish.json teach name and fam, wfam where WoRMS holds other families; families imr and genera imr). A tagged entry must have its name and fam here, and its sub-entries their name (the build stops otherwise). An entry of another source keeps its name and fam in tools/fish_source.json.",
  "  pdf (teaching nodes only, any source): the section tokens (family heading) of the IMR reference PDF whose species the entry should hold, the build's cross-check against the PDF.",
  "  sl: the presentation's slide numbers for the entry or sub-entry (the families' slide references and the look lines' source).",
  "  cues, look ([teach id, how to tell it apart]), phase: short English from the IMR fish presentation (its slides: sl).",
  "species: {species id (tools/fish_source.json species): its fields}. sl: the slide of the presentation that names the species. A species the source does not hold stops the build.",
  "  pdf: the pages of the IMR reference PDF (the EventMeasure list) that hold the species: it marks the species as the PDF's (366), and is the IMR list that confirms it near Dauin (rule C8). Only then: common (the PDF's common name, never corrected), sec (its section, the family token of its heading) and cs (its rank on the PDF's cheatsheet, 24 species). A species of another source (dauin, wink) keeps its common name and its src in the base.",
  "  src (only \"slides\"): the species the presentation names and the PDF does not; a species with no pdf."
],
